                "description": "Complete unshaded upward-opening parabola with black coordinate axes, positive-axis arrowheads, blue curve with arrows on both branches, exact root labels, y-intercept label 2 and a marked, labelled vertex. No student graph is supplied in the question.",
                "mathematics": "y=x^2+4x+2=(x+2)^2-2; vertex (-2,-2); roots -2-sqrt(2) and -2+sqrt(2); y-intercept (0,2). The plotted equation uses vertex form without changing the coordinate scale or labelled values.",
                "answerVisibility": "solution-only"
